    "body": "Having the same issue, and i agree with @josepharhar on what i think is happening. \n\nA workaround is to track the state manually: \n```js\n    let open = false;\n\n    const content = document.getElementById(\"myPopover\");\n    const button = document.getElementById(\"myButton\");\n\n    content.addEventListener(\"toggle\", (e) => (open = e.newState == \"open\"));\n\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n      if (open) {\n        content.hidePopover();\n      } else {\n        content.showPopover();\n      }\n    });\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
