    "updated_at": "2025-11-06T20:47:56Z",
    "body": "So I think this is actually a bug in the algorithms. The \"right\" way to do this should be this:\n\n```\n<div id=popover1 popover>popover</div>\n<div onclick=popover1.togglePopover({source: this})>test</div>\n```\n\nI.e. the `source` parameter should connect the trigger to the popover, which should then get used during the light dismiss algorithm. Currently, light dismiss uses the [\"topmost clicked popover\" algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#topmost-clicked-popover), which calls [\"nearest inclusive target popover\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#nearest-inclusive-target-popover), and that uses [\"popover target element\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#popover-target-element) to find invokers to include in the light dismiss algorithm. Unfortunately, that last algorithm just checks for `popovertarget`. Interestingly it doesn't even look for `commandfor` combined with `command={something}-popover`.\n\nChecking this repro (https://jsbin.com/bohagab/edit?html,output), it seems that both Chromium and Gecko DO properly look at the command invokers and do the right thing. (WebKit doesn't implement `commandfor` yet.) None properly handle the imperatively-added `source` from the `togglePopover()` call. It feels like \"popover target element\" should be updated to include both `commandfor` popover invokers (to match browser behavior) and also include the \"reverse\" concept of the [popover trigger](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#popover-trigger). I say \"reverse\", because we'd need to store a pointer on the invoking/source element pointing to the popover. That might get tricky - it might be possible to have one invoker pointing to more than one open popover.\n\nIn the meantime, the currently-supported way to do this is to use either of the declarative ways to invoke popovers:\n```\n<div id=popover2 popover>popover</div>\n<button popovertarget=popover2>test 2</button>\n\n<div id=popover3 popover>popover</div>\n<button commandfor=popover3 command=\"toggle-popover\">test 3</button>\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
